<title>CANADA: Canada July department store sales rise on month.</title>
<headline>Canada July department store sales rise on month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian department stores sales rose a seasonally adjusted 0.7 percent in July from June to C$1.19 billion, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>In unadjusted data, year-over-year sales in July rose 1.8 percent to C$1.02 billion.</p>
<p>Sales at major stores fell 4.2 percent in July from the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>Consumer spending in discount stores rose 6.7 percent from the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>Discount stores have now enjoyed year-over-year gains in sales every month for 17 months.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Mary Beth Garneau, Retail Trade Section, Industry Division, 613-951-3556.)</p>
<p>-- Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745</p>
